When an order had no datatrans_payment_transaction row, fetchRow() returned false and reading
$transactionRow['transaction_mode'] raised a warning; Magento's error handler turned it into an
exception, the cron rethrew it as CronException and the whole run stopped. Use ?? so the existing
"no transaction id -> continue" guard skips such orders.

diff --git a/Cron/OutageRecoveryChecker.php b/Cron/OutageRecoveryChecker.php
index d22a337..83b7e82 100644
--- a/Cron/OutageRecoveryChecker.php
+++ b/Cron/OutageRecoveryChecker.php
@@ -162,7 +162,10 @@ class OutageRecoveryChecker
                     );
 
                     $transactionId = $transactionRow['transaction_id'] ?? null;
-                    $mode = $transactionRow['transaction_mode'];
+                    //BEGIN PATCH
+//                    $mode = $transactionRow['transaction_mode'];
+                    $mode = $transactionRow['transaction_mode'] ?? null;
+                    //END PATCH
 
                     if (!$transactionId) {
                         continue;
